---
id: skillet-blistered-cauliflower-florets
title: Skillet-Blistered Cauliflower Florets
category: modular_cooked_veg

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 440

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Place @frozen-cauliflower-florets{500%g} in a #skillet with 2 tbsp water. Cover with a tight-fitting lid and turn the heat to medium-high. Steam for ~steam-time{4.5%min} until the florets are fully thawed and pliable.

Remove the lid, turn the heat up to high, and let any remaining water cook off completely for ~evaporate-time{90%sec}.

Once the pan is dry, drizzle @avocado-oil{2%tsp} directly over the cauliflower along with @kosher-salt{0.5%tsp}, @garlic-powder{0.33%tsp}, and @black-pepper{0.25%tsp}. Toss well and sauté undisturbed for ~sear-time{3.5%min} until golden-brown and charred on the edges.

Divide equally into 2 meal prep containers (220 g cooked yield each) and let cool before sealing.
